            <ArticleTitle>[Invagination of the small intestine due to leiomyoma. A case report of echographic diagnosis].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>95-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors describe a case of intestinal invagination caused by leiomyoma of the small intestine. They make the diagnostic difficulties of the disease apparent and stress the importance of abdominal echography in cases of acute abdominal disorders.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
